-- Busted runs with -c during mutation. LuaCov would then save `luacov.stats.out`
-- on exit, inside the project (the unmutated baseline) or inside a worker
-- overlay (every mutant run). The standard mutator requires both trees to stay
-- byte-for-byte unchanged while workers are reused, and it never reads these
-- statistics: coverage is collected from the explicit configuration that
-- crapper writes under target/coverage. Send the default statistics to the
-- null device so a test run leaves no file behind.
local separator = package.config:sub(1, 1)
return {
  statsfile = separator == '\\' and 'NUL' or '/dev/null',
}
